DEC X.500 Directory Service V1.3 on OpenVMS AXP

Network Resource Issues:

Users want their network resources to be accessible from anywhere in their
multivendor networks, whether for end user access or for system/application
access. Today, however, information is stored on a per-network or
per-application basis, and this makes it hard to find and access.

System managers also need to manage these resources easily -- adding,
deleting, or modifying services as networks change to adjust to topology or
organizational changes. Instead, the information they need is scattered,
stored in separate directories and multiple databases, all with different
access mechanisms.

Thus current technology is limited in its ability to support the needs of
all applications, but the new X.500 technology can support these needs. It
provides a single directory for locating, accessing, and managing
information about network services, resources, and people.

Product Description:

X.500 directories are already used by a number of applications, and users
are starting to deploy X.500 across their networks. Because these networks
are multiplatform, users are requiring a choice of platform for their X.500
server and access from all platforms for their X.500 clients.

With the V1.3 release of DEC X.500 Directory Services (SPD 40.77.xx),
support is now being provided for the OpenVMS AXP platform, and the existing
support for the DEC OSF/1 AXP and OpenVMS VAX platforms has been upgraded to
cover the latest versions of the operating systems and DECnet/OSI. The
ULTRIX RISC platform is also supported, so X.500 V1.3 aligns a common
version across four platforms.

In V1.3, new functionality has been introduced to aid in the administration
of directory data. The new bulk load and unload features enable the loading
of the directory from external script or data files as well as a mechanism
to perform bulk moves or edits of data already stored within the directory.
This greatly reduces the effort required to make administrative changes in
the directory.

For further information, please consult the following articles in Digital's
Customer Update: "DEC X.500 Directory Service V1.0," May 10, 1993; "DEC
X.500 Directory Service V1.1," September 27, 1993; "DEC X.500 Directory
Service V1.2," November 22, 1993; and "InfoBroker Server for OSF/1 AXP and
Client for Windows," April 12, 1994.

Availability and Ordering:

DEC X.500 Directory Service V1.3 is available now. Each DEC X.500 Directory
Service starter kit includes both DEC X.500 Directory Server V1.3 and DEC
X.500 Administration Facility V1.3.

All platforms use the Consolidated Software Distribution CDROMs. For
information on other options refer to the SPD.

