TL820 5.2 Tbyte Digital Linear Tape Library

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Based on industry leadership DLT technology, new library provides high
   capacity and performance in small footprint

o  Significantly lowers entry price for large scale unattended backup and
   archiving

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The TL820 digital linear tape (DLT) library is the newest member of
Digital's family of near-online automated storage products, providing up to
5.2 Tbytes of storage for unattended backup operations, archiving, large
scale data storage, and video-on-demand applications. The TL820 DLT library
uses three high performance TZ87 tape drives for unsurpassed data integrity
and high capacity (up to 20 Gbytes compressed per cartridge).

The TL820 DLT library can be a significant component in a user's overall
plan to provide unattended access to ever-increasing amounts of data while
holding down costs and thus improve productivity substantially. Its key
features supporting this position are as follows:

o  High capacity -- The basic TL820 stores the equivalent of 35,000 9-track
   tapes, or an 80 million page filing cabinet, ensuring that all of an
   organization's data can be online for timely retrieval.

o  Flexibility -- Up to five towers can be connected together into a
   seamless, virtual library through the use of an innovative pass-through
   mechanism, providing up to 26 Tbytes of data storage for true
   enterprise-wide data storage.

o  Compactness -- The TL820 has a footprint of slightly over nine square
   feet (less than one square meter). This is considerably less than that of
   competing products and non-automated alternatives.

o  High performance -- Based on the TZ87 drives, the TL820 provides a
   throughput of up to 2.5 Mbytes per second per drive, or 7.5 Mbytes per
   second per library, ensuring that both data storage and retrieval are
   accomplished quickly.

o  Leadership data integrity and reliability -- The TZ87 drives used by the
   TL820 provide the highest data integrity and reliability of any tape
   drives available today, assuring a high degree of availability and
   uninterrupted operation.

o  Low cost -- The TL820 represents a new price point for high performance,
   multiterabyte libraries, making it easier than ever to implement
   unattended storage operations.

Users often compare optical jukeboxes with tape libraries. Digital believes
that the random access capabilities of optical drives make them best suited
for applications requiring access to relatively small objects, such as some
hierarchical storage applications, permanent archives, and document imaging.
Tape libraries are best suited for the storage and retrieval of large
objects, especially when the object's data organization is sequential, such
as a backup data set or seismic or telemetry data.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The TL820 DLT library is available now from Digital and its business
partners for DEC OSF/1 AXP, OpenVMS VAX, and OpenVMS AXP systems.

