Pacer for DEC OSF/1 AXP V2.6

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Introducing Macintosh file and print services for DEC OSF/1 AXP systems

o  Resale of Pacer file and print server software

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Macintosh users need to participate in corporate information exchanges, have
access to expanded workgroup LANs, and integrate with other workgroup LANs
regardless of the underlying network operating system technologies.

Pacer for DEC OSF/1 AXP V2.6 server software provides seamless integration
between DEC OSF/1 servers and Macintosh clients. It is the result of an
agreement between Digital and Pacer Software, Inc., to resell Pacer's
AppleTalk file and print software. Under the agreement, a PATHWORKS for
Macintosh client license grants users the right to access DEC OSF/1 AXP,
ULTRIX RISC, or OpenVMS VAX servers.

Pacer for DEC OSF/1 AXP V2.6 server software includes the following
components:

o  PacerShare, an AFP 2.1 compliant AppleShare file server and the AppleTalk
   network transport, gives Macintosh users access to the data storage
   capacity of DEC OSF/1 systems with the convenience and transparency of
   Macintosh systems.

o  PacerPrint, a LaserWriter 8.0 compatible (PAP) print server, enables
   Macintosh users to send print jobs to DEC OSF/1 PostScript printers,
   freeing the Macintosh from the delays associated with printing directly
   to a LaserWriter. PacerPrint also provides DEC OSF/1 users with the
   ability to print to the same PostScript printers.

o  PacerAdmin lets administrators create, examine, modify, and delete file
   server users, groups, volumes, and spoolers from any Macintosh on the
   network.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

Pacer for DEC OSF/1 AXP V2.6 software is available now from Digital and its
business partners. One of the PATHWORKS for Macintosh client licenses listed
below is required for each Macintosh client that uses the Pacer software.

The CDROM version of the media and documentation kit will be available in
September.

