DECdfs V2.0 for OpenVMS Systems

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Support for OpenVMS AXP

o  New, client-only license options

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

OpenVMS users often have a need to access data that resides on OpenVMS
systems other than their own local system. Without the ability to access
this data, they may be forced to duplicate it -- which is both inefficient
and error-prone.

DECdfs V2.0 for OpenVMS systems (SPD 28.78) is a DECnet and DECnet/OSI
layered product that provides users and applications with transparent, high
performance access to remote OpenVMS files and disks. DECdfs consumes less
CPU resources than standard DECnet file access.

DECdfs systems can act as servers, or clients, or both. An OpenVMS system
running DECdfs server software can make its file resources available to
systems running DECdfs client software. File resources accessible through
DECdfs can range from an individual file to a master file directory and all
of its underlying subdirectories and files on a disk volume.

With the introduction of V2.0, DECdfs for OpenVMS software now supports
OpenVMS AXP systems as well as OpenVMS VAX systems. The various new features
can be summarized as follows:

o  An ongoing ability to share file resources transparently between OpenVMS
   systems.

o  The addition of AXP system support. DECdfs V2.0 supports OpenVMS AXP V1.5
   and V6.1.

o  Support for OpenVMS VAX V5.5-2, V6.0, and V6.1.

o  Support for DECnet and DECnet/OSI access on both OpenVMS VAX and OpenVMS
   AXP systems.

o  A new, client-only license option. Users can now choose to license their
   OpenVMS systems to function as DECdfs clients. The full-function license
   will continued to be offered.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

DECdfs V2.0 for OpenVMS systems is available now through local Digital sales
offices and Digital's business partners. A license is required on each
OpenVMS system that registers available directories or files for access and
use by DECdfs clients, and on each OpenVMS system that accesses and uses the
directories or files on a DECdfs server.

Separate client-only and full-functionality licenses are offered. The full-
functionality license grants the right to use both the client and server
capabilities of the DECdfs V2.0 for OpenVMS software. License prices vary by
tier.

The media kits contain DECdfs client and server software for both VAX and
AXP systems.

DECdfs for OpenVMS software and documentation are also included in Digital's
CDROM Software Library for OpenVMS AXP (QA-03X*A-H8) and the OpenVMS VAX
Consolidated Distribution (QA-VWJ8A-A8).

