POLYCENTER Print Queue Manager V4.3

Product Description:

POLYCENTER Print Queue Manager V4.3 (SPD 62.76.01) eases print queue
management in an enterprise, enabling operations personnel to set up printer
queues on multiple systems from a central point. A menu driven operations
tool, it defines and maintains many different print queue parameters from a
central point, such as LAT, DQS, physically attached, PostScript, and LPS
printers. V4.3 supports DCPS V1.0 and DCPS-PLUS software, which is required
on the target nodes where the queues are set up.

POLYCENTER Print Queue Manager also can be used jointly with POLYCENTER
System Watchdog. The System Watchdog monitors each queue and triggers an
action routine (for example, automatic restart), using the Print Queue
Manager setup for that queue, whenever the queue is found in a "paused,"
"stalled," or "stopped" state.

Benefits:

o  POLYCENTER Print Queue Manager saves time and facilitates operations
   management by centrally storing print queue definitions and device
   parameters.

o  It minimizes the risk of errors and increases productivity for print
   queue setups.

o  It simplifies the creation, update, and deletion of print queues on any
   client node within the managed domain, such as a datacenter or a complete
   enterprise. This is achieved using the client/server approach.

o  It lets users view, print, or list all print queue definitions, along
   with a queue activity report, and it includes a queue balancing feature.

