       	   The replacement products, the DECNIS and DEC WANrouter products,
           either have or will have DEC OSF/1 AXP and MS-DOS kits for load
           and management in these environments.

       	   The retiring software for the DEMSA based products will continue
           to be supported until the end of December 1995.

       (2) The RWZ01 and RWZ21 5.25" and 3.5" discs are being retired in
           line with current trends in the optical disc marketplace. The
           associated media and accessories will remain active.

       	   The replacement product for the RWZ01 will be the RWZ52 5.25" 1.2
           GB magneto-optical disc drive, which offers better performance
           solutions at a lower price. As a multifunctional drive capable of
           reading and writing 600 Mbyte and 1.2 Gbyte media, the RWZ52 will
           protect your disc drive investments.

       (3) Now that Digital has transitioned development and support of DEC
           @AGlance products to Intuitive Technology Corporation, it has
           begun a retirement process for the DEC @AGlance V1.0 software
           products listed above.

       	   @AGlance/IT V2.0, a new release of @AGlance software offered by
           Intuitive Technology, contains all the functionality provided in
           Digital's DEC @AGlance V1.0, plus key features and enhancements.
           Under its migration plan, Intuitive Technology will offer
           @AGlance/IT V2.0 software and documentation plus an upgrade
           license at a discounted price to all Digital users with a current
           Software Product Services contract. Users who do migrate can
           purchase a support agreement directly from Intuitive Technology.

       	   Digital will continue to support DEC @AGlance V1.0 in accordance
           with the terms of the service contract, but not beyond July 31,
           1995. Warranty users will receive support throughout their
           initial warranty agreement.

       	   If users decide upon an immediate transfer to Intuitive
           Technology services, they should contact their local Digital
           representative to request termination of their existing DEC
           @AGlance service agreement.

       (4) Digital is transitioning ongoing development, sales, service, and
           support of the DECrti product to KineticSystems Corporation.

       	   Initially, KineticSystems will ship Digital's DEC Realtime
           Integrator V3.0a on OpenVMS VAX and RISC ULTRIX systems.
           Thereafter, KineticSystems will ship the product as the KSC
           Realtime Integrator, or KSCrti V3.1, with plans to support the
           OpenVMS AXP and DEC OSF/1 AXP platforms.

       	   DECrti users will have the opportunity to purchase an update
           license from KineticSystems and receive new versions of the
           Realtime Integrator products.

       	   Support for Digital's V3.0a will continue through Digital's
           Customer Support Centers in accordance with the terms of service
           contracts through June 30, 1995. Warranty users will receive
           support throughout their initial warranty agreement.

       	   KineticSystems will provide a migration path to enable DECrti
           users to convert to KineticSystems software products. With the
           purchase of a KineticSystems support contract, the company will
           ship a new license, license keys, software media, and
           documentation updates directly to a user's address. At that time
           users can ask Digital to cancel their service contract for V3.0a.

       (5) Note that this is not a platform retirement: Digital is
           simplifying the product set to focus on packages that buying
           patterns indicate users want. If a desired package does not exist,
           users can configure one through the system building block
           approach.

