DEC 3000 Model 700 AXP and Reduced-Price Model 600 AXP

HIGHLIGHTS

o  New Model 700 provides high performance, with graphics benchmark of over
   15.1 XMARKS

o  Reduced price on Model 600 makes it fastest workstation under $20,000

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Users are requiring higher levels of performance, at lower costs, for their
technical and financial applications. Digital is responding to these
requirements with the DEC 3000 Model 700 AXP workstation, offering top
performance for a cost effective price. The system includes a 21 inch color
monitor, 64 Mbyte memory, 1 Gbyte disk, and CDROM. The Model 700 is the
first of a new generation of TURBOchannel based workstations.

Digital also is lowering the price of the DEC 3000 Model 600 AXP
workstation. Now the repriced Model 600 is the fastest workstation under
$20,000 from any vendor.

BENEFITS

o  As economic, business, and scientific models have become larger and more
   complex, they have exceeded the address limits of 32 bit hardware,
   requiring slower, multistep access or the use of 64 bit computers.
   Digital's Alpha AXP systems have full 64 bit architectures and 64 bit
   operating systems and can handle increasing demands well into the next
   century.

o  DEC 3000 systems, running such applications as MCAD, ECAD, GIS, and
   scientific visualization, allow users to solve the larger problems they
   are now required to handle.

o  Digital's price/performance leadership results in cost savings for its
   users, while upgrades from current Alpha AXP workstations to the new
   Model 700 protect their investment.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The DEC 3000 Model 700 will be available in August 1994 with DEC OSF/1 AXP
V2.1 and OpenVMS AXP V6.1. The system building blocks (120/240 V) listed
below require the addition of graphics, disks, monitors, and keyboards. All
packaged systems shown are Northern Hemisphere, 120/240 V.

Digital is offering upgrades from the Model 600 family to the new Model 700
family with a field service installed board swap. Users upgrading from a
Model 400 will receive a complete new system box via the ADVANTAGE-UPGRADE
program; see the accompanying article in this issue.

OpenVMS AXP V6.1 or DEC OSF/1 AXP V2.1 media and documentation kits are
available as separate line items. Although all systems with a disk have
factory installed software, at least one media and documentation kit per
site is recommended.

For compute intensive applications requiring more than single processor
performance, these systems can be combined into Alpha AXP UNIX clusters
using LSF compute share software.

