WARRANTY

The HSD30 product carries a three-year limited hardware warranty. The first
year of the warranty is provided onsite at the basic service level, and
years two and three are on a return-to-Digital basis. The product warranty
is honored worldwide and can be enhanced with Digital's supplemental
services.

SERVICES

The full range of Digital service offerings for the HSD30, including
installation, basic maintenance, and DECService maintenance, is available
and recommended.

TECHNICAL DATA

Supporting up to 18 storage devices in redundant controller subsystems and a
maximum of 21 devices for single HSD30 configurations, the HSD30 DSSI array
controller can draw on the same StorageWorks power and packaging options as
the HSJ series of subsystems. It is housed in the standard BA350-MA/MB shelf
for SW500 and SW800 series enclosures, with up to two controllers per shelf
for redundancy and failover on the same DSSI bus. In the SW500/SW800
enclosures, device shelf connection is provided with three independent SCSI
cables.

Initially, the following devices are being supported on the HSD30:

                             Solid
        Disk                 State
        Drives    Tapes	     Disks    CDROMs

        RZ26      TLZ06      EZ51R    RRD42
        RZ26L     TLZ06L     EZ54R    RRD43
        RZ28      TZ86       EZ58R    RRD44
        RZ28B     TZ87/N
                  TZ867
                  TZ877

The SW800 datacenter cabinet supports up to 18 building block shelves and
four controller shelves. The SW500 cabinet can hold a total of 10 shelves,
including one or two controller shelves.

The HSD30 controller comes with HS Operating Firmware V1.5. With this
version of the firmware, a maximum of four HSD30s is being supported per
DSSI bus, along with HSD05s, RF series disks, and TF series tape devices.

The HSD30 Array Controller is supported with limitations on OpenVMS VAX
V5.5-2 and later and on OpenVMS AXP V1.5 and 6.0. These limitations consist
of a lack of ERF (Error Reporting Format) and related translations support.

The supported OpenVMS VAX processors are the VAX 4000, 6000, 7000, and
10000. The supported OpenVMS AXP processor is the DEC 4000.

